                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—The acting commander of the second zone is
                    Gen. Col. José Ma Raugel. The acting commander of the third zone is (Jen. Col.
                    José del Valle. The commander of the fourth zone is Brig. Gen. Emiliano Lajero.
                    The officer in command of the Laredo line is Col. Luis Ceron, of the cavalry.
                    The officer in command of the line between Mier and Guerrero is Gen. Col. L.
                    Garcia.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note</hi>.—On the night of December 13, 1892, 60 men
                    of the twenty-sixth battalion left Monterey for Laredo by rail, and on the
                    morning of the same day 40 men of the thirteenth regiment marched for the same
                    place by ordinary road. On the 21st of the same month 100 foot soldiers left for
                    the same place by rail.</p>
